<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on Dec 20.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on Dec 20.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		 Position	     Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Orient ExpressI    SLD Dec 10	    1,200	Cambodia</p>
<p>Chip Sam	     ETD Dec 17	    1,265	N.Korea</p>
<p>Orient ExpressI    ETA Dec 19-20	 1,200	Cambodia</p>
<p>Dien Bien	    ETA Dec 20	    7,000	Japan</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	  ETR Dec 20	   14,300	Japan</p>
<p>Zang San	     ETA Dec 23		700	N.Korea</p>
<p>Great Concert	ETA Dec 25	   13,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Pakarti Sembilan   ETA Dec 28	    5,250	Indonesia</p>
<p>Ivan Makarin	 ETA Dec 28	   17,850	Japan</p>
<p>Manii II		  N/A		  2,000	Singapore</p>
<p>Sangthai Venus	  N/A		  1,500	Singapore</p>
<p>Yon Pung Ho	  ETA Dec 29	   12,000	Sri Lanka</p>
<p>Kum Gang	     ETA Dec 31	   12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Bangpo		 L/CAN Jan 2-7	 2,300	Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure, ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
</text>
